notes.body:
Except if I missed something, when I'm looking at the caller in `dissect_rdp_rdstls` calling `dissect_rdp_fields` with `authReqFields==null` can't happen. The two consecutive switch prevent that, but clang is unable to compute that invariant.
```C
authReqFields = NULL;
switch(pduType) {
case 2:
    authReqFields = XXXX
    break;
....
}

...

switch(pduType) {
    case 2:
       dissect_rdp_fields(tvb, offset, pinfo, tree, authReqFields, pdu_length-6);
...
}
```
Unusual data in the tvb gives early exit and no call to `dissect_rdp_fields`.

